# Log in first with http/auth.http (Owner), then run these in the same VS Code session.
# Every write needs an Origin header equal to the server's own scheme and host.

### List products (page, pageSize, includeArchived for the Owner)
# Expect 200 { items, total, page, pageSize }
GET http://localhost:3000/api/products?page=1&pageSize=20

### Create a product (Owner only)
# Expect 201 with sku "BRS-5KG" (spaces removed, uppercase) and minStock 0
POST http://localhost:3000/api/products
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "brs 5kg", "name": "Beras 5 kg", "unit": "pcs" }

### Duplicate SKU
# Expect 409 { "code": "CONFLICT", "message": "SKU sudah dipakai." }
POST http://localhost:3000/api/products
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "BRS-5KG", "name": "Duplikat", "unit": "pcs" }

### Invalid unit
# Expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST http://localhost:3000/api/products
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "X1", "name": "x", "unit": "kg", "minStock": -1 }

### Get one product (replace the id)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/products/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000

### Edit a product (Owner only)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/products/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Beras 10 kg", "minStock": 10 }

### Archive a product (archived: false restores it)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/products/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "archived": true }
